Description: Samsung Gear VR Controller as mouse and keyboard
 A user-level daemon that connects to a Samsung Gear VR Controller over
 Bluetooth Low Energy and turns it into a virtual input device: the
 touchpad moves the pointer and scrolls, the buttons act as mouse buttons
 and keys. The mapping is configurable in ~/.config/vrcontroller/config.toml.
 .
 The daemon pairs the controller automatically and serves a live status
 page on http://127.0.0.1:8765/.
 .
 The package adds a udev rule that lets the user logged in at the local
 seat create virtual input devices through /dev/uinput, and loads the
 uinput module at boot.
